--- body ---

## Context

M1b overlays a stable navigation schema on the immutable M1a inventories from
[[0832]]. It does not manufacture a homogeneous project population. Canonical
IDs and a small common taxonomy are decided once; only source-documented
`same_as` and `component_of` relations enter the catalogue. Probable matches
remain a separate counted result rather than a research backlog. This is the
first bounded catalogue milestone of [[0725]].

## First test

A fixture contains an exact duplicate documented by a source locator, a
source-documented component, and a plausible but unproven name/capacity match.
The build emits respectively `same_as`, `component_of`, and one unchanged row
in `possible_matches`. The probable match does not alter canonical membership,
counts or M1a bytes. Removing the evidence locator makes either certain
relation fail validation.

## Actions

1. Freeze the common record taxonomy and deterministic canonical-ID rules.
2. Build an overlay catalogue without editing or deleting M1a inventory rows.
3. Admit only `same_as` and `component_of` with source ID, locator and concise
   justification.
4. Export all other candidate relations to a separate `possible_matches` table
   with country, candidate IDs, reason and evidence references; do not resolve
   them through new research.
5. Display catalogue and unresolved-match counts without presenting objects
   from different source layers as a comparable statistical population.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Canonical-ID and taxonomy rules are versioned, deterministic and tested
- [ ] M1a tables remain byte-identical and every catalogue record links back to their rows
- [ ] Every admitted relation is `same_as` or `component_of` with source ID and locator
- [ ] `possible_matches` is separate, non-operative and counted by country
- [ ] No new source acquisition or match-resolution campaign occurs
- [ ] Catalogue, relation and uncertainty downloads reproduce from the frozen M1a release

## Out of scope

Resolving `possible_matches`, following newer sources, updating lifecycle
states, reconciling CRS/IATI, payments or physical assets are M2 work.
